/-!
# Dimension of quotients by partial systems of parameters

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 02IE, `lemma-elements-generate-ideal-definition`;
Tag 07DU, `definition-ideal-definition`
(blueprint: lem-per-partial-parameters-quotient-dimension).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

/-- Quotienting a Noetherian local ring by the first `i` members of a system of `d`
parameters gives dimension `d - i`. The index `j : Fin d` represents the parameter `a_{j+1}`.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 02IE, `lemma-elements-generate-ideal-definition`,
with ideals of definition as in Tag 07DU, `definition-ideal-definition`
(blueprint: lem-per-partial-parameters-quotient-dimension).

Proof:
1. Fix `1 ≤ i ≤ d`. Let `I` be the ideal generated by the first `i` parameters,
`B = A/I`, and `n` the image of the maximal ideal. The quotient map is surjective
with kernel `I` by `def-weil-pbc-algebra-hom-quotient`. The ideal correspondence
preserves prime ideals, maximal ideals and strict inclusions. Since `I` is contained
in the maximal ideal, `B` is nonzero local, and images of generators of inverse-image
ideals make it Noetherian (`def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring`). Lifting prime chains gives
`0 ≤ e = dim B ≤ d` (`def-weil-pbc-krull-dimension-ring`). Heights of maximal ideals
in local rings equal their ring dimensions, so these heights are `d` and `e`.
2. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-height-quotient-bound`, represented by
`Ideal.height_le_height_add_encard_of_subset`, to the first `i` generators and the
maximal ideal of `A`. The generator set has cardinality at most `i`, giving `d ≤ e + i`.
3. Let `K` in `B` be generated by the images of the remaining `d - i` parameters.
The composite quotient has kernel the full parameter ideal `J`, so `B/K` is isomorphic
to `A/J` and is nonzero. Every prime containing `J` contains its radical, the maximal
ideal, and hence equals that maximal ideal. Thus `B/K` has exactly one prime and
has dimension zero; its unique prime has height zero.
4. Apply the same height-quotient bound in the Noetherian local ring `B` to `K` and
its maximal ideal. The image prime has height zero, giving `e ≤ d - i`. This also
applies when `i = d`, since the bound permits an empty generating family.
5. Combine the two inequalities, using `i ≤ d`, to obtain `e = d - i`.
When `d = 0`, there is no index `i` in the stated range. -/
theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_span_initial_parameters
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (d : ℕ) (hdim : ringKrullDim A = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) (a : Fin d → A)
    (ha : ∀ j : Fin d, a j ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (hrad : (Ideal.span (Set.range a)).radical = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (i : ℕ) (hi : 1 ≤ i) (hid : i ≤ d) :
    ringKrullDim (A ⧸ Ideal.span (a '' {j : Fin d | j.val < i})) =
      ((d - i : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  sorry
